There is an intrinsic, "You can detect detrimental food", which can be
gained by reading a blessed scroll of food detection or by casting the
spell detect food at Expert (or possibly Skilled) level.  This allows
you to detect tainted, poisonous, acidic, hallucinogenic, pertificant,
lycanthropic, or slimed food prior to eating it and gives you the
option to not eat it. However, regarding ROTTEN food, the spell
appears to allow you to detect rotten food SOME of the time as well,
even the partially eaten food ration that was the last piece of food
you ate.  I'm not a code diver, so I don't know any more than that.
Furthermore, this intrinsic only lasts until you detect a piece of bad
food, after that you lose the intrinsic.

